 "verdict": "RUNG: at r=2 the per-position values reproduce selection_mode's stored s_far/s_near to within 0.0988 across 9 arms (tolerance 0.18). Same lattice as F123, so the ladder extends it rather than replacing it. PRIMARY, branching by radius on the settled pool: binary|freq_matched r2=1.124/r3=1.264/r4=1.193/r6=1.636; binary|semantic r2=0.878/r3=1.353/r4=1.321/r6=1.421; binary|uniform r2=1.000/r3=1.283/r4=nan/r6=0.120; colours|freq_matched r2=1.057/r3=1.663/r4=1.670/r6=1.757; colours|semantic r2=0.900/r3=1.040/r4=1.115/r6=1.017; colours|uniform r2=1.017/r3=1.011/r4=1.195/r6=1.558; digits|freq_matched r2=1.113/r3=1.488/r4=1.754/r6=2.435; digits|semantic r2=0.979/r3=1.561/r4=1.752/r6=2.434; digits|uniform r2=1.030/r3=1.383/r4=1.795/r6=2.724. 9 of 9 arms reach the criticality threshold of 1 within r <= 6: crossing radii binary|freq_matched=2, binary|semantic=3, binary|uniform=3, colours|freq_matched=3, colours|semantic=4, colours|uniform=4, digits|freq_matched=3, digits|semantic=3, digits|uniform=3. Widening the window DOES buy back what a smaller alphabet costs, and the mean-field trade s = 1/r is usable as a design rule. SECONDARY, decay of s_pos with distance (ratio between consecutive positions at the largest radius): binary|freq_matched=0.9375, binary|semantic=0.89, binary|uniform=4.4523, colours|freq_matched=0.9203, colours|semantic=0.8634, colours|uniform=1.0116, digits|freq_matched=0.9588, digits|semantic=1.0182, digits|uniform=0.9502. A ratio near 1 means the sum grows with r; well above 1 means it converges and no window size crosses. BOUNDARY: EleutherAI/pythia-410m step4000, T = 0.7, N = 48, 64 windows per position. This measures the CONSTRUCTION, not a model property. At large r the lattice drifts toward ordinary conditional generation and stops deserving the name CA; where that line sits is not something this run can decide.",
